    "content": "Fran McCaffery is the head coach of the University of Pennsylvania (Penn) men's basketball team, hired in April 2025. In his first season (2025–26), he led the 14th-seeded Quakers to the NCAA Tournament after an 88–84 overtime win in the Ivy League Championship. Watch this video to see the official introduction of Fran McCaffery as the head coach of Penn Basketball:59sCBS PhiladelphiaYouTube • Apr 7, 2025 59s Key Details About Coach McCaffery: Career Achievement: He is one of only a few NCAA Division I coaches to lead five different programs (Lehigh, UNC Greensboro, Siena, Iowa, and Penn) to the NCAA Tournament. Background: McCaffery is a 1977 graduate of La Salle College High School and returned to coach at his alma mater, having previously coached at Iowa for 15 seasons. Playing Style: His teams are known for a fast-paced, high-intensity style. 2025-26 Season: He guided the Quakers to an 18–11 record and an Ivy League title. This video features an interview with Coach McCaffery about his journey and preparations for the NCAA Tournament:56s97.5 The FanaticYouTube • Mar 17, 2026 56s Note: There is also a distinct Penn State women's basketball program which hired Tanisha Wright in March 2026.",
